# UI Improvements & Screen Dimmer Plan

## Context

Single-screen Expo radio app. Layout: Header → CategoryTabs → StationList + MiniPlayerBar.
Playback via `useRadioPlayer()` / `RadioPlayerService`. Hook signal: `playerState.isPlaying`.
Screen may turn off during playback; audio continues via track-player background service.

## UI Improvement 1: Pinned Mini Player Bar ✅ DONE

**Problem:** ControlPanel scrolls off-screen when browsing the station list.

**Completed:**
- `components/MiniPlayerBar.tsx` — pinned to bottom inside `SafeAreaView`, visible when `currentStation` is set
- Reuses `togglePlayPause` and `stop` from `App.tsx`
- Bottom safe area via `useSafeAreaInsets()` from `react-native-safe-area-context` (required for Android `edgeToEdgeEnabled`)
- **Refresh (list-aligned):** brand avatar + `getStationDisplayName()`, top accent line + brand tint background
- **Status:** LIVE badge + `EqualizerBars` when playing; pulsing dot when loading; grey paused text; error tint + `retry` action
- **Controls:** brand-colored play/pause; stop replaced with subtle **X close** icon
- **Spotify-style glass:** mini player **overlays** station list (`App.tsx` absolute positioning) so background content shows through; iOS uses `expo-blur` `BlurView`, Android uses semi-transparent frosted layer (native blur optional after `expo run:android`)
- Station title format: `{brand} · {display name}`
- i18n: `live`, `retry`, `close`

**Optional later:** Expandable volume; tap-to-expand now-playing sheet

## UI Improvement 2: Finish i18n in ControlPanel ✅ DONE

**Problem:** ControlPanel uses hardcoded Korean (`연결 중...`, `볼륨`) while other components use `useLanguage()`.

**Completed:**
- `useLanguage()` wired into `ControlPanel.tsx`
- Loading and volume labels use `t.loading`, `t.volume`
- Play/pause/stop buttons use `t.play`, `t.pause`, `t.stop` as accessibility labels

**Follow-up (optional):** Map `RadioPlayerService` error messages through i18n in the UI layer

## Feature: Screen Dim via Overlay ~~REMOVED~~

**Removed:** Background playback via track-player makes overlay dim unnecessary. Deleted `useScreenDimmer`, `ScreenDimOverlay`, and `screenDimmedHint` i18n.

## UI Improvement 3: Galaxy Tab Landscape Layout ✅ DONE

**Problem:** App is portrait-only; Galaxy Tab should default to landscape with a split layout.

**Completed:**
- `expo-screen-orientation` — phones lock portrait, tablets lock landscape on launch
- `utils/deviceUtils.ts` — tablet detection (shortest side ≥ 600dp)
- `hooks/useDeviceLayout.ts` — `isLandscapeTablet` for responsive layout
- `hooks/useOrientationLock.ts` — runtime orientation lock by device class
- `components/LandscapeDecorPanel.tsx` — gradient decor panel with animated wave rings when playing
- `App.tsx` — landscape tablet: radio UI in left panel (~480dp), decor fills remainder
- `app.json` orientation `"default"` + Android manifest `unspecified` (JS handles lock)

**Layout:** Left panel = Header → CategoryTabs → StationList + MiniPlayerBar. Right = branded decor with now-playing card.

## Feature: Background Playback & Media Controls ✅ DONE

**Problem:** Playback was tied to `expo-av` + `expo-keep-awake`. Switching apps or turning the screen off was unreliable on Galaxy; no notification or lock-screen controls.

**Goal:** Play radio while using other apps. Stable background audio on Galaxy. Notification + lock-screen play/pause/stop.

**Approach:** `react-native-track-player@4.1.2` with Expo dev build (`expo run:android`). `RadioPlayerService` migrated from `expo-av` to track-player. UI (`useRadioPlayer`, ControlPanel, MiniPlayerBar) unchanged.

**Completed:**
- `react-native-track-player@4.1.2` requires **New Architecture disabled** (`newArchEnabled: false`) — v4 is incompatible with TurboModules
- `services/playbackService.ts` — remote play/pause/stop handlers
- `services/trackPlayerConfig.ts` — notification capabilities (play/pause only; stop is in-app)
- `services/RadioPlayerService.ts` — track-player queue, live streams, podcast seek/progress
- `index.ts` — `TrackPlayer.registerPlaybackService()`
- `app.json` — `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK`, iOS `UIBackgroundModes: audio`
- Android manifest + `strings.xml` notification channel (`ML Radio FM`)
- Live stream notification/lock-screen uses static wave-ring artwork (`assets/live-artwork/frame-00.png`)
- `appKilledPlaybackBehavior: StopPlaybackAndRemoveNotification` — swipe app away from recents stops playback and removes notification; background play while multitasking still works
- ~~`PlayerKeepAwake` / `expo-keep-awake`~~ removed — screen auto-off during playback; audio via track-player
- Expo **dev builds** auto-enable keep-awake on Android (`withDevTools`); `App.tsx` calls `deactivateKeepAwake(ExpoKeepAwakeTag)` on launch

**Pending QA (real device):**
- Screen-off playback, station switch, phone call / audio focus on Galaxy
- Optional: notification channel i18n + network reconnect on drop

## UI Improvement 4: Compact Station List with Brand Colors ✅ DONE

**Problem:** Station cards felt tall and meaningless — same green background, redundant "한국/해외 라디오" meta, weak playback feedback.

**Completed:**
- `components/StationList.tsx` — card layout replaced with compact rows (hairline dividers, ~44px row height)
- Removed redundant per-row type meta; category tabs already filter by broadcaster
- `utils/categoryUtils.ts` — `getStationBrand()` (KBS/MBC/SBS/BBS/YTN/AR/FM label + color), `getStationDisplayName()` (strip broadcaster prefix)
- Left **brand avatar** circle per row using broadcaster colors from `categoryInfo`
- Current station: left **accent bar** + tinted row background in brand color
- `components/EqualizerBars.tsx` — compact 4-bar equalizer animation for playing state; pause icon when paused; spinner when loading
- Removed `selectedCategory` prop from `StationList` (prefix logic no longer needed)
- **Section headers** on "All" tab — `SectionList` with sticky KBS / MBC / SBS / Other / International groups via `groupStationsIntoSections()`

**Optional later:**
- Add `frequency` / `genre` fields to `stations.ts` for richer subtitles

